  "summary": "A typical two-piston hydraulic bicycle disc-brake caliper. Fluid from a hose pushes opposed pistons that clamp pads onto a rotor (commonly 160 mm). A pad pin and spring hold the pads in the body; a bleed nipple vents air; two bolts fix the body to a post-mount fork or frame. One degree of freedom as the inboard piston advances.",
  "approximate": true,
